# Accepted quote deviations, with reasons. One per line: <verdict>|<quote prefix>|<reason>
# Reviewed 2026-09-05. Add an entry only when the difference is provably NOT the
# book's error -- never to silence a mismatch you have not run down.
#
# Context for every entry below: the chapters were written from ccel.org, but the
# machine-check corpus was pulled from biblestudytools.com, which prints the SAME
# Henry text with scripture citations in Arabic numerals where CCEL uses Roman
# ("John iii. 14, 15" vs "John 3:14"). That formatting difference breaks a
# substring match mid-quote. Each line below was individually re-fetched from the
# CCEL page and confirmed to be Henry's text exactly as printed there.
MISS|All the first-born are mine; for on the day that I smote|KJV text Henry prints as his lemma for Num 3; present on the CCEL page verbatim. Confirmed 2026-09-05.
DRIFT|Thus were the Lord's ministers themselves then kept in fear|Runs on into "1 John i. 1" (CCEL) / "1 john 1 1" (corpus); wording identical. Confirmed against CCEL 2026-09-05.
MISS|The Lord bless thee, and keep thee|The Aaronic blessing as Henry prints it (Num 6:24-26); present on the CCEL page verbatim. Confirmed 2026-09-05.
DRIFT|Certain men were defiled by the dead body of a man|Differs only by "ch. xix. 11" (CCEL) vs "ch. 19:11" (corpus). Confirmed against CCEL 2026-09-05.
DRIFT|This teaches us...the particular care God takes of his people|Differs only by "Ps. cvii. 7" (CCEL) vs "Ps. 107:7" (corpus). Confirmed against CCEL 2026-09-05.
MISS|Our Saviour has told us so (John iii. 14, 15)|Differs only by Roman-numeral citation style; CCEL prints exactly this. Confirmed 2026-09-05.
DRIFT|The apostle describes Balaam's sin here to be that he ran greedily|Exact match on CCEL; the corpus copy carries an HTML-link whitespace artifact at the citation. Confirmed 2026-09-05.
MISS|What God had said to Moses (ch. xxvi. 53)|Quoted from CCEL, which prints "ch. xxvi. 53"; the corpus prints "ch. 26 53". Confirmed 2026-09-05.
DRIFT|For, when rivalry arose concerning the priesthood|CCEL 的 HTML 把腳註 187（"literally, every tribe being written according to its name."）夾在 "with the name" 與 "of the tribe" 之間；語料抓取一併帶入，書稿引的是革利免的正文。逐字核對 anf01.ii.ii.xliii 2026-09-05。
DRIFT|What think ye, beloved? Did not Moses know beforehand|CCEL 的 HTML 在 "and that" 與 "the name of the true and only God" 之間夾入頁碼 "17"；書稿引的是正文，未含該頁碼。逐字核對 anf01.ii.ii.xliii 2026-09-05。
MISS|There shall come a star out of Jacob, and a leader shall rise in Israel|CCEL 的 HTML 在 "and a" 與 "leader" 之間夾入頁碼 "423"（分隔過早，比對器判為 MISS 而非 DRIFT）；書稿引的是愛任紐正文，未含該頁碼。逐字核對 anf01.ix.iv.x 2026-09-05。
MISS|Making a start with these wells, run through all Scripture|來源掃描本在印刷排版斷行處保留連字號 "Scrip-\nture"、"com-\nparison"（archive.org selectionsfromco0000orig 與 earlychurch.org.uk 兩份獨立掃描在同一位置斷字，字句一致）；比對器不做斷行連字合併，故判為 MISS。逐字核對 Tollinton, *Selections...*, SPCK 1929, p. 88 2026-09-05。
